   "semantic_assessment": "The first timeout10s/abort/stream overflow latches a reason, initiates POSIX group kill or bounded async Windows taskkill/fallback, and starts the2s settlement backstop. Close and the backstop use that latched reason if they win settlement. The separate child error callback can instead start settlement first with generic bridge launch failed, even after a reason was latched. This is not managed-runner verified containment.",
